      "message": "`std::move` (below) does not make any sense for `const\u0026`. That\u0027s because the semantics of move involves modifying the source object for \"extracting\" the handles value from it w/o making a copy. If it\u0027s not allowed to modify the source object, `move` degrades into making a copy.\n\nI would suggest `BtProfileHandles` a public type in `Module`. Then we can take it here as an rvalue: `Module::BtProfileHandles\u0026\u0026 btHandles`. This will connect it nicely with `Module::getBtProfileManagerHandles`—you can just pass what it returns to the constructor directly. And here we can move values out from the tuple. That should be a proper use of `move`.",
